## Why This Is Asked

This question probes practical DR design: cross-region replication, active-active components, idempotent processing, and observable validation under real outage scenarios.

## Key Concepts

- DR and RTO/RPO
- Pub/Sub exactly-once delivery
- Cloud Run warm-standby
- Spanner multi-region vs Cloud SQL replication
- Dataflow streaming to BigQuery
- Per-environment isolation
- Observability and chaos testing

## Code Example

```javascript
// Node.js Pub/Sub subscriber skeleton with idempotent dedup logic
const {PubSub} = require('@google-cloud/pubsub');
const dedupe = new Set();
exports.receiveEvent = async (msg, context) => {
  const id = msg.attributes?.messageId || msg.id;
  if (dedupe.has(id)) {
    msg.ack();
    return;
  }
  dedupe.add(id);
  // process
  msg.ack();
};
```

## Follow-up Questions

- How would you verify RTO/RPO in production and CI/CD?
- What metrics and alarms would you define to detect a failover failure?

## Why This Is Asked

This question evaluates practical data privacy workflow design on GCP, testing understanding of DLP integration, environment isolation, and robust data processing patterns.

## Key Concepts

- Cloud Storage event-driven processing with Cloud Functions
- Cloud DLP API for PII classification and redaction
- Per-environment BigQuery dataset isolation and governance
- Checksum-based idempotence and processing manifest tracking
- Structured logging with correlation_id for comprehensive observability

## Code Example

```javascript
// Node.js example using DLP
const {DlpServiceClient} = require('@google-cloud/dlp');
const client = new DlpServiceClient();

async function redactPII(data) {
  const [response] = await client.redactContent({
    parent: `projects/${process.env.PROJECT_ID}/locations/global`,
    item: { value: data },
    deidentifyConfig: {
      infoTypeTransformations: {
        transformations: [{
          infoTypes: [{ name: 'ALL_BASIC' }],
          primitiveTransformation: {
            replaceWithInfoTypeConfig: {}
          }
        }]
      }
    }
  });
  return response.item.value;
}
```
